---

<BaseLayout title="Recommended Attire" description="Recommended attire for bellydance and Spanish dance classes with Reischa.">
	<PageHero slot="hero" image={attireHero} title="Recommended Attire" showTitle />

	<section class="section">
		<h2>Belly Dance</h2>
		<p><strong>Clothing &mdash;</strong> Be comfortable and able to move freely. I recommend jazz pants, exercise pants, cropped, fitted dance tops, or leotards. A hip scarf without coins is preferred for class work.</p>
		<p><strong>Shoes &mdash;</strong> Not required, however you may prefer to wear jazz or lyrical shoes, and some street shoes may work for class.</p>
		<p><strong>Discouraged &mdash;</strong> Please do not wear jeans, non-dance skirts, street shoes, &amp; other restricting articles.</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<h2>Spanish Dance</h2>
		<p><strong>Clothing &mdash;</strong> For most classes, any modest exercise or dance wear is suitable. Close to exams, a black flamenco skirt, tights, and a black long-sleeved leotard is required.</p>
		<p><strong>Shoes &mdash;</strong> Character shoes and some dress shoes are ok to start. Flamenco shoes are preferred, and will be most suitable for exams &amp; performance.</p>
		<p><strong>Discouraged &mdash;</strong> Please do not wear jeans, non-dance skirts, street shoes, &amp; other restricting articles.</p>
	</section>

